{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTrace_peel_physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTrace_peel_physical","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidTower.lean#L134-L141","doc":"**Move II at the forced weight.** With `w = (1, q²)` — the weight the peel itself forces —\nthe scalar is `q³ · wi`, i.e. convention D's `z = q³/(q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTrace_peel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTrace_peel","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidTower.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**Markov move II, on braids.** Adding a strand and one crossing multiplies the normalised\ntrace by the peel scalar `z · wi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.heckeRep_braidTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.heckeRep_braidTower","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidTower.lean#L96-L118","doc":"**The tower square commutes.** Representing a braid after adding a strand is the same as\nadding the strand in the algebra — two group homomorphisms agreeing on generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTower_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTower_gen","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidTower.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidTower","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidTower.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The braid tower** `B_{m+1} → B_{m+2}`: add a strand on the right, leaving every crossing\nwhere it was. Its only input is `coxA_castSucc`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidGen_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower.braidGen_braid","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidTower.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**The defining relation, in the group.** The alternating words agree in `Art(M)` — which is\nwhat `PresentedGroup` was quotiented by, read back through `map_altProd`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}